{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "16", "x": 0.9080829955905043, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.0256602530131315, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 2", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.154855388251959, "w": 0.2545169675210174, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Question 14 – 26, which are based on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.18674558158013102, "w": 0.8271744286771318, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "to Britain", "x": 0.4510011202901702, "y": 0.24038783476038392, "w": 0.14071088547419278, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Mark Rowe investigates attempts to reintroduce elms to Britain", "x": 0.1959618393919942, "y": 0.27867834878074654, "w": 0.6494478569875318, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "A", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3169466071795277, "w": 0.02121427120700475, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Around 25 million elms, accounting for 90% of all elm trees in the UK, died", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.3169466071795277, "w": 0.7662288799876724, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "during the 1960s and '70s of Dutch elm disease. In the aftermath, the elm, once so", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.34527695725366536, "w": 0.8264233308655577, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "dominant in the British landscape, was largely forgotten. However, there's now", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.37360738277058797, "w": 0.8259464873054115, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "hope the elm may be reintroduced to the countryside of central and southern", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4019377328447256, "w": 0.8263062473683126, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "England. Any reintroduction will start from a very low base. 'The impact of the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.43026808291886326, "w": 0.8260336335161456, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "disease is difficult to picture if you hadn't seen what was there before,' says Matt", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.45859847071439336, "w": 0.8262948670984402, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Elliot of the Woodland Trust. 'You look at old photographs from the 1960s and it's", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48680524550666543, "w": 0.8264662888212019, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "only then that you realise the impact [elms had] ... They were significant, large", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.515135595580803, "w": 0.8264944831834983, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "trees ... then they were gone.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5434659833763332, "w": 0.30204809999217735, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "B", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5817342229144181, "w": 0.020206412464245704, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "The disease is caused by a fungus that blocks the elms' vascular (water,", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.5817342229144181, "w": 0.7655352986751828, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "nutrient and food transport) system, causing branches to wilt and die. A first", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6100646107099483, "w": 0.8262126420854888, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "epidemic, which occurred in the 1920s, gradually died down, but in the '70s a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6383949607840859, "w": 0.8258158705142642, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "second epidemic was triggered by shipments of elm from Canada. The wood came", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6667624287084543, "w": 0.8261640452573853, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in the form of logs destined for boat building and its intact bark was perfect for", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6950927787825919, "w": 0.8264059016234109, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the elm bark beetles that spread the deadly fungus. This time, the beetles carried", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7234231288567294, "w": 0.8262514990429808, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "a much more virulent strain that destroyed the vast majority of British elms.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7517535543736521, "w": 0.7699812932969288, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "C", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7898734356749919, "w": 0.02101269433220525, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Today, elms still exist in the southern English countryside but mostly only", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.7898734356749919, "w": 0.7662045815736207, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in low hedgerows between fields. 'We have millions of small elms in hedgerows", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8182038611919146, "w": 0.8260337360410994, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "but they get targeted by the beetle as soon as they reach a certain size,' says", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8465342112660521, "w": 0.8266415039672543, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Karen Russell, co-author of the report 'Where we are with elm'. Once the trunk of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8748893065736769, "w": 0.8268042110689426, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the elm reaches 10-15 centimetres or so in diameter, it becomes a perfect size for", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9032196566478146, "w": 0.8262047476640458, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "beetles to lay eggs and for the fungus to take hold. Yet mature specimens have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9315500067219521, "w": 0.8258594436196312, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}